## Project structure

```
MovieTicketingSystem/
├── pom.xml                     Maven settings and the MySQL driver
├── db.properties.example       copy to db.properties and add your MySQL login
├── database/
│   ├── schema.sql              creates the movie_ticketing database (11 tables)
│   ├── sample-data.sql         demo staff, customers, movies, showtimes and bookings
│   └── test-queries.sql        checks, must-fail tests and the queries the DAOs use
├── docs/                       class diagram and ER diagram (PDF and draw.io)
└── src/main/java/com/movieticketing/
    ├── MovieTicketingSystem.java   starts the app (opens the login screen)
    ├── model/       User, Customer, Cashier, Manager, Movie, Showtime, Seat,
    │                Booking, Ticket, Payment, CardPayment, CashPayment,
    │                Setting, SalesReport, Printable and the enums
    ├── dao/         DatabaseConnection and one DAO per table
    │                (User, Movie, Showtime, Seat, Booking, Setting, Report)
    ├── service/     BookingService: holding seats, age check, payment
    ├── exception/   SeatUnavailable, Payment, Authentication, Validation
    ├── util/        PasswordUtil (salted SHA-256 password hashing)
    └── ui/          LoginFrame, RegisterFrame, the three dashboards,
                     SeatMapPanel and TicketTypeDialog
```

Screens talk to the service and DAO classes, and only the DAOs talk to MySQL. Screens never contain SQL.

## OOP concepts used

| Concept | Where |
|---|---|
| Encapsulation | Every model class keeps its fields private, with getters, setters and validation |
| Inheritance | `Customer`, `Cashier` and `Manager` extend `User`. `CardPayment` and `CashPayment` extend `Payment`. Every window extends `JFrame`, and `SeatMapPanel` extends `JPanel`. |
| Abstraction | `User` and `Payment` are abstract classes with abstract methods |
| Polymorphism | `user.createDashboard()` opens the right screen for each role. `payment.process()` behaves differently for card and cash. |
| Interface | `Ticket` and `SalesReport` implement `Printable` |
| Composition | A `Booking` is made of `Ticket`s and has one `Payment` |
| Custom exceptions | Four checked exceptions, for example `SeatUnavailableException` when two people pick the same seat |
| Inner classes | The manager dashboard's tabs (`MoviesTab`, `ShowtimesTab`, `StaffTab`) |

## Security

- Passwords are stored as salted SHA-256 hashes, never as plain text.
- Every query uses `PreparedStatement`, which blocks SQL injection.
- The database login lives in `db.properties`, which is never committed.
- The database itself rejects a seat sold twice for the same show (`UNIQUE (showtime_id, seat_id)`).

## Diagrams

The `docs/` folder holds the class diagram (model classes, data access, user interface) and the ER diagram, as PDFs and as draw.io files you can edit at [app.diagrams.net](https://app.diagrams.net).
